update public.pages set html = $qd_customer_terms$<style id="qdmf">html,body{overflow-x:hidden;max-width:100%}.body{overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word}.body table{display:block;width:100%;overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch}.body img{max-width:100%;height:auto}</style><h1>Terms of Service</h1><div class="muted">For customers using QuotesDone to request quotes and reveal suppliers.</div><div class="card"><p>These Terms and Conditions (&quot;Terms&quot;) govern your use of the QuotesDone platform as a customer. QuotesDone is the online platform operated by QuotesDone Technologies, a Sole Establishment licensed by the Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism (E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275; Commercial Register No. 2883503), Dubai, United Arab Emirates (&quot;QuotesDone&quot;, &quot;we&quot;, &quot;us&quot;). QuotesDone is an online B2B sourcing marketplace operated in Dubai, United Arab Emirates. By creating an account, submitting a request for quotations, or paying a reveal fee, you accept these Terms. Acceptance by electronic means (including click-acceptance) is valid and binding under Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021 on Electronic Transactions and Trust Services.</p><h2>1. Definitions</h2><p>&quot;Platform&quot; means the QuotesDone website, applications and services. &quot;Customer&quot;, &quot;you&quot; means the business or individual requesting quotations. &quot;Supplier&quot; means a vetted third-party provider that submits quotations. &quot;Inquiry&quot; means a request for quotations you submit. &quot;Quote&quot; means an anonymised quotation from a Supplier. &quot;Reveal&quot; means unlocking the identity and contact details of a chosen Supplier. &quot;Reveal Fee&quot; has the meaning in clause 4.</p><h2>2. The service and how anonymous quoting works</h2><p>QuotesDone lets you describe a job (by text, voice, photo or drawing). Our system structures your request and matches it to vetted Suppliers, who submit competing quotations on an anonymised basis - you can compare prices and scope without any party&#x27;s identity being disclosed.</p><p>QuotesDone is a marketplace and facilitator only. It is not a contractor, supplier, agent or party to any contract for the works. Quotes are prepared by independent Suppliers who are solely responsible for their pricing, scope and performance.</p><h2>3. Account and eligibility</h2><p>You must provide accurate registration details and keep your account secure. You are responsible for activity under your account. You must be authorised to procure the services you request.</p><h2>4. Reveal Fee (3%, no cap) and VAT</h2><p>Comparing quotes is free. A Reveal Fee becomes payable only when you choose to reveal a Supplier you wish to engage.</p><p>The Reveal Fee is three percent (3%) of the value of the selected quotation. There is NO maximum cap on the Reveal Fee. The exact amount is shown to you clearly before you confirm payment.</p><p>The Reveal Fee is paid through the Platform (card or Apple Pay) and is charged once per reveal. Revealing a Supplier does not create any contract between you and QuotesDone for the underlying works; it unlocks the Supplier&#x27;s identity so you may contract with them directly.</p><p>All Reveal Fees are stated exclusive of VAT. Where QuotesDone is registered for VAT, VAT at the prevailing rate (currently 5%) is added and shown on a valid tax invoice issued under Federal Decree-Law No. 8 of 2017. Before you confirm payment you are shown the exact Reveal Fee in AED as a single total amount, inclusive of any applicable VAT, with no hidden or further charges for the reveal.</p><h2>5. Refunds, immediate performance and complaints about non-responsive suppliers</h2><p>You expressly request that QuotesDone perform the Reveal immediately upon payment, and you acknowledge that the service &mdash; disclosure of the Supplier&#39;s identity and contact details &mdash; is fully performed and delivered electronically at the moment of Reveal. Once the Reveal has been delivered, any right to cancel before delivery is exhausted and the Reveal Fee is earned. The Reveal Fee is not automatically refundable, and there is no self-service refund.</p><p>If, after a Reveal, the Supplier does not respond to you, you do not need to do anything for the clock to start: QuotesDone tracks every Reveal from the moment you pay. If the Supplier has not responded within three (3) working days of your payment, QuotesDone chases the Supplier on your behalf, copying you. If there is still no response by the fifth (5th) working day, the case goes to QuotesDone&#39;s CEO for a final call. You may also raise a complaint through the Platform at any time; contacting the Supplier in writing (for example by email) and copying supplier@quotesdone.com puts your own attempt to reach the Supplier on record.</p><p>If the Supplier has failed to respond both to you and to QuotesDone within five (5) working days of your payment and does not respond to the CEO&#39;s final call, the Reveal Fee is refunded. The refund is the full Reveal Fee you paid (3% of the quotation value); QuotesDone deducts nothing from it. Every refund is decided by QuotesDone&#39;s CEO and recorded against your refund case reference, which we quote to you when we confirm the outcome; no refund is automatic and there is no self-service refund. Once a refund is issued, banks and card issuers usually take seven (7) to fourteen (14) working days to show it on your statement. Working days are Monday to Friday, excluding UAE public holidays.</p><p>A Supplier is treated as having &quot;responded&quot; if they reply by any reasonable means, including the on-platform message thread, telephone, email or WhatsApp. No refund, re-match or credit is due where: the Supplier has responded; you have already engaged, contracted with, or contacted the Supplier outside the Platform other than the complaint email described above; the same Supplier was revealed to you previously; you are dissatisfied with the Supplier&#39;s price, quotation or terms; or you have simply changed your mind. QuotesDone may decline or limit repeated requests that indicate misuse of this policy.</p><p>Nothing in this section removes any right you have that cannot be excluded under the Consumer Protection Law of the United Arab Emirates.</p><h2>6. Anonymity and non-circumvention</h2><p>Anonymity is the core of the service. You agree not to seek, accept or use any means to identify or contact a Supplier off-platform before a paid reveal, and not to use the Platform to obtain Supplier identities and then transact off-platform to avoid the Reveal Fee.</p><p>Quotes and any attachments are provided for your evaluation only and must not be shared in a manner that circumvents the Platform.</p><h2>7. Customer obligations and acceptable use</h2><p>You agree to provide accurate information, use the Platform lawfully, not submit fraudulent or abusive inquiries, and not misuse, scrape, or interfere with the Platform or other users&#x27; data.</p><h2>8. No warranty on supplier works; independent contractors</h2><p>Suppliers are independent third parties. QuotesDone does not guarantee the quality, legality, safety or completion of any works, nor the accuracy of any Quote. Any contract for the works is solely between you and the Supplier. You are responsible for your own due diligence before engaging a Supplier.</p><h2>9. Liability</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by UAE law, QuotesDone&#x27;s total liability arising out of or in connection with the Platform is limited to the total Reveal Fees you paid in the three (3) months preceding the event giving rise to the claim. QuotesDone is not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for the acts, omissions or works of any Supplier.</p><p>Nothing in these Terms limits or excludes liability for fraud, gross negligence, death or personal injury caused by negligence, or any liability that cannot be limited or excluded under UAE law, including non-waivable consumer rights.</p><h2>10. Data protection</h2><p>QuotesDone Technologies (E-Trader Licence No. 1633275), the operator of the Platform, is the data controller. We process personal data in accordance with the UAE Personal Data Protection Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021), on the lawful bases of performance of a contract, our legitimate business interests, and your consent where required, and we may use service providers (including outside the UAE) under appropriate safeguards. You may exercise your rights of access, correction, deletion and objection, and raise complaints, as set out in our Privacy Policy.</p><p>Electronic communications: we send transactional messages (one-time passwords, request and quote notifications, and account or payment confirmations) as part of providing the service; these are not marketing. We send marketing or promotional messages by email or SMS only with your consent, and you may opt out at any time. Electronic communications are handled in line with the rules of the Telecommunications and Digital Government Regulatory Authority (TDRA) and the Electronic Transactions and Trust Services Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021.</p><h2>11. Consumer rights</h2><p>Where the Consumer Protection Law (Federal Law No. 15 of 2020) and Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023 apply, your statutory rights are preserved and prevail over any inconsistent provision of these Terms.</p><h2>12. Suspension and termination</h2><p>QuotesDone may suspend or terminate access for breach of these Terms, suspected fraud or circumvention, or as required by law. You may stop using the Platform at any time; fees already incurred remain payable.</p><h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2><p>QuotesDone may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be notified through the Platform or by email and take effect prospectively.</p><h2>14. AI-generated content and platform outputs</h2><p>QuotesDone uses automated and AI-based tools to interpret your requirements, generate bills of quantities and cost estimates, standardise and compare quotations, and power support assistants. These outputs are provided for convenience only, may contain errors, and are not professional, engineering, legal or financial advice. You must verify any such output before relying on it, and QuotesDone is not liable for loss arising from reliance on automated outputs. QuotesDone does not guarantee that you will receive any quotation, or any particular number, price or quality of quotations.</p><h2>15. Payments, the payment processor, no escrow, and chargebacks</h2><p>The Reveal Fee is charged by card or Apple Pay through our payment processor, Stripe, which is certified to the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS); QuotesDone does not store your full card details and is not liable for processor outages or errors. All amounts are in UAE Dirhams (AED) unless stated otherwise. Because a Reveal delivers value (the supplier&#39;s identity and contact details) immediately, the Reveal Fee is non-refundable except as set out in section 5 (Refunds and non-responsive suppliers). Initiating a chargeback or payment dispute after a Reveal, other than for a genuine unauthorised transaction, is a breach of these Terms and entitles QuotesDone to suspend your account and recover the disputed amount and reasonable costs.</p><p><b>No escrow; QuotesDone does not hold your money.</b> The only payment QuotesDone collects is its own Reveal Fee, charged through Stripe at the moment of Reveal. QuotesDone does not hold, escrow, receive, transmit or process any payment for the goods, works or services quoted between you and a Supplier. All payment for the actual job is arranged and settled directly between you and the Supplier, on terms agreed between you. QuotesDone is not a party to that contract and does not act as an escrow agent, payment institution, money-services business or stored-value provider in respect of those funds, and accepts no responsibility for the payment, non-payment, performance or quality of any job.</p><h2>16. Electronic acceptance and records</h2><p>Ticking the acceptance box or continuing to use the Platform constitutes a valid and binding electronic acceptance of these Terms under the laws of the United Arab Emirates. QuotesDone&#39;s records, including its acceptance logs and the signed acceptance certificate it generates, are admissible and, absent manifest error, conclusive evidence of the terms you accepted and when.</p><h2>17. Compliance and communications</h2><p>You warrant that you are not subject to sanctions and that your funds are lawful, and you will comply with applicable anti-money-laundering and sanctions laws. You consent to receive service and transactional communications, and (unless you opt out) promotional communications, by email, SMS and WhatsApp, and may unsubscribe from promotional messages at any time. Any feedback or suggestions you provide may be used by QuotesDone freely and without obligation.</p><h2>18. Complaints and dispute resolution</h2><p>If you have a complaint, please contact QuotesDone first at management@quotesdone.com or through the Platform. Every complaint receives a ticket number that you can track at <a href="/complaints/status/">quotesdone.com/complaints/status</a>. We will acknowledge your complaint within two (2) working days and give a substantive response within ten (10) working days, as set out in our <a href="/complaints/">Complaints Policy</a>. If your complaint is not resolved to your satisfaction, you may escalate it to the Consumer Rights channels of the Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism (DET), including the Dubai Consumer app, or to the UAE Ministry of Economy consumer hotline (800 1222). This complaints procedure does not affect your statutory rights or the governing law and jurisdiction set out below.</p><h2>19. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2><p>This document is governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates, including the Commercial Transactions Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 50 of 2022), the Personal Data Protection Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021), the Electronic Transactions and Trust Services Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021), the Consumer Protection Law (Federal Law No. 15 of 2020) and its Implementing Regulation (Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023), and the Civil Transactions Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 25 of 2025, in force from 1 June 2026, replacing Federal Law No. 5 of 1985). The courts of Dubai have jurisdiction.</p><h2>20. Contact</h2><p>This Platform is operated by QuotesDone Technologies, E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275, Commercial Register No. 2883503, Dubai, UAE. Questions about these Terms can be sent to info@quotesdone.com or management@quotesdone.com.</p><h2>Permitted use &amp; platform protection</h2><p>These provisions form part of the Customer Terms (Version 6, effective 14 September 2026) and are accepted at registration.</p><p>By registering and using QuotesDone, you agree that you will not: (a) access or use the Platform to build, design, benchmark or assist any competing product or service; (b) copy, scrape, harvest, republish or extract any supplier data, pricing, content or other materials from the Platform by any automated or manual means; or (c) reverse-engineer, decompile or replicate any part of the Platform&#39;s software, matching logic, anonymisation outputs or document templates. All such data and materials remain the exclusive property of QuotesDone.</p><p>Any breach of this clause entitles QuotesDone to immediate suspension or termination of the account, liquidated compensation of AED 10,000 per incident as a genuine pre-estimate of loss, recovery of any further proven losses, and injunctive relief to stop ongoing breach.</p></div><script>/*qdarfix*/(function(){if((localStorage.getItem('qd_lang')||'en')!=='ar')return;function run(){var c=document.querySelector('.crumb');if(c)c.innerHTML='<a href="/">الرئيسية</a> › القانوني › شروط الخدمة';document.querySelectorAll('.dochead .meta').forEach(function(m){m.innerHTML=m.innerHTML.replace('Version','الإصدار').replace('Last updated','آخر تحديث');});}if(document.readyState!=='loading')run();else document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',run);})();</script>$qd_customer_terms$
 where slug = 'legal_terms_body';

update public.pages set html = $qd_supplier_agreement$<style id="qdmf">html,body{overflow-x:hidden;max-width:100%}.body{overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word}.body table{display:block;width:100%;overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch}.body img{max-width:100%;height:auto}</style><h1>Supplier Agreement</h1><div class="muted">For suppliers registering and quoting on QuotesDone. Version 9 · governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. Agreement &amp; acceptance</h2><p>This Supplier Agreement (the "Agreement") is a binding contract between QuotesDone Technologies, a Sole Establishment licensed by the Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism (DET) under E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275, Commercial Register No. 2883503, Dubai, United Arab Emirates, which operates the QuotesDone platform ("QuotesDone", "we", "us", "the Platform"), and the registering business ("you", "the Supplier"). By ticking the acceptance box during sign-up, or by using the Platform, you confirm that you have read, understood and agree to be bound by this Agreement. Ticking the box constitutes a valid electronic signature under UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021 on Electronic Transactions and Trust Services. If you are accepting on behalf of a company, you warrant that you are authorised to bind that company.</p>
<h2>2. Definitions</h2><ul><li><b>Customer</b> — a user who requests quotations through the Platform.</li><li><b>Quotation Value</b> — the total price the Supplier quotes for a job, exclusive of VAT.</li><li><b>Reveal</b> — the point at which a Customer pays to unlock and select a Supplier for a job; a job is "won" upon Reveal.</li><li><b>Subscription Fee</b> — the annual supplier subscription fee described in clause 6.</li><li><b>Working Days</b> — days other than Saturdays, Sundays and UAE public holidays.</li></ul>
<h2>3. Eligibility &amp; registration</h2><p>To register you must be a lawfully established business in the UAE holding a valid trade licence covering the services you offer, and the individual registering must be authorised to act for that business. You agree to provide accurate, current and complete company, licence, tax (TRN), bank and contact information and to keep it updated.</p>
<h2>4. Account &amp; security</h2><p>Access is secured by one-time-code verification. You are responsible for activity on your account and for keeping access credentials and the registered email secure. Notify us immediately of any unauthorised use.</p>
<h2>5. The service</h2><p>QuotesDone is an anonymous quotation marketplace and technology platform. Customers post jobs and receive anonymised quotations; the identities of Customer and Supplier are released only through the Platform after a Reveal. QuotesDone is an introducer and facilitator only; it is not the contractor, is not a party to the contract for the work, and does not supervise, perform or guarantee any work.</p>
<h2>6. Registration &amp; subscription fees</h2><p>Supplier registration is <b>free of charge for the first 1,000 businesses to register</b> on the Platform, permanently. From the <b>1,001st registration</b> a subscription fee of <b>AED 1,000 per year</b> applies, payable annually in advance. QuotesDone will give at least 30 days' notice and seek re-confirmation of acceptance before introducing or varying the fee, as set out in the Amendments section; continued use of the Platform after the effective date constitutes acceptance. The subscription fee, once paid, is non-refundable except as expressly stated at the time.</p>
<h2>7. No supplier commission</h2><p><b>QuotesDone charges the Supplier no commission on any job won through the Platform</b> — not on the Quotation Value, not on the amount finally invoiced, and not on repeat work with the same Customer. The Platform is funded by the subscription fee in clause 6 and by a fee payable by the Customer at Reveal. QuotesDone reserves the right to introduce a supplier commission in future only on at least 30 days' notice and re-confirmation of acceptance as set out in the Amendments section; no commission is or becomes payable under this version of the Agreement.</p>
<h2>8. Payment terms</h2><p>Where a Subscription Fee is payable under clause 6, it is payable annually in advance, by card or by bank transfer, on the renewal date of the Supplier's account. QuotesDone may issue an invoice or statement for amounts due; payment is not conditional on receipt of an invoice. All amounts are in AED unless stated. Separately, the Customer — not the Supplier — pays QuotesDone a reveal fee of <b>3% of the Quotation Value</b> at the moment of Reveal. Nothing is deducted from, or charged on, the amount the Customer pays the Supplier for the work.</p>
<h2>9. Late payment</h2><p>If a Subscription Fee is not received by its due date, QuotesDone may, after giving the Supplier notice and a further <b>7 Working Days</b> to pay, suspend the Supplier's account until payment is made. Unpaid Subscription Fees are debts due and payable and may be recovered through the competent UAE courts. Overdue amounts carry interest at the single rate set out in clause 31. QuotesDone holds no funds for the Supplier (it collects only its own fees), so no set-off against held sums applies.</p>
<h2>10. Anonymity &amp; non-circumvention</h2><p>The Platform's value depends on anonymity. The Supplier must not, during anonymised stages or in on-platform chat, share or solicit phone numbers, email addresses, links, WhatsApp or other messaging or social-media handles, or otherwise attempt to take dealings off the Platform or bypass the Reveal. Any such disclosure or circumvention entitles QuotesDone to suspend the Supplier's account and to a liquidated sum of <b>AED 10,000 per incident</b>, agreed as a genuine pre-estimate of the lost platform value and lost subscription revenue, which is the sole monetary remedy for that incident (QuotesDone will not separately claim general damages for the same act). For a first and evidently inadvertent technical breach, QuotesDone may at its discretion issue a written warning instead of applying the sum. The Supplier acknowledges that this sum is agreed compensation (liquidated damages) under the UAE Civil Transactions Law, which a competent court may adjust to the actual loss.</p>
<h2>11. Supplier obligations &amp; conduct</h2><p>The Supplier shall: honour every quotation it submits and any agreed timeline; respond to revealed Customers professionally and promptly; deal honestly and not engage in collusion, bid-rigging or price manipulation; and comply with all applicable UAE laws, including the Consumer Protection Law (Federal Law No. 15 of 2020) and health-and-safety requirements. QuotesDone, for its part, will operate the Platform in accordance with its own obligations as a digital marketplace under that law and its executive regulations.</p><p><b>Winning a job &amp; response time.</b> When a Customer reveals and selects the Supplier, the Supplier is notified that it has won the job and the Customer is given the Supplier&#39;s contact details (by SMS, WhatsApp and/or email) so the Customer can make contact. The Supplier must begin responding to the Customer within <b>5 working days</b> of the Reveal. If the Supplier has not responded within 3 working days of the Reveal, QuotesDone chases the Supplier, copying the Customer; if there is still no response by the 5th working day the case goes to QuotesDone&#39;s CEO for a final call, and if the Supplier does not respond to that call the Customer&#39;s reveal fee is refunded and the non-response charge in clause 33 applies. Repeated non-responsiveness may lead to suspension. QuotesDone is notified of every such case.</p>
<h2>12. Quotations &amp; the supplier–customer contract</h2><p>A quotation is the price the Supplier wishes to receive for the work. A quotation is valid for <b>30 days</b> from submission unless the Supplier refreshes or withdraws it before Reveal, and the Supplier is bound by a quotation that is revealed within that validity period. The contract for the work itself is solely between the Supplier and the Customer, on terms they agree; QuotesDone is not a party to it and is not responsible for either party's performance, payment or conduct.</p>
<h2>13. Trade licence &amp; regulatory compliance</h2><p>The Supplier must maintain a valid UAE trade licence and any approvals required for its trade, and upload renewals before expiry. QuotesDone verifies every Supplier before it can be matched: the mandatory six (business name, mobile number, email address, trade licence, company profile and signed acceptance of this Agreement) must be complete, and the trade licence number, issuing authority and expiry date are checked, within three (3) Working Days of complete documents. QuotesDone does not verify the Supplier&#39;s workmanship, solvency or insurance (where an insurance policy is uploaded, only its expiry date is tracked). These checks are published at <a href="/how-we-verify/">How we verify suppliers</a>. QuotesDone may suspend, unverify or remove accounts that are unverified, expired, inaccurate or misrepresented.</p>
<h2>14. Ratings &amp; feedback</h2><p>The Supplier acknowledges that Customers and QuotesDone may rate and review performance, and that such ratings may be displayed. Ratings reflect user feedback and are not endorsements by QuotesDone.</p>
<h2>15. Intellectual property</h2><p>All intellectual property in the Platform belongs to QuotesDone. The Supplier grants QuotesDone a non-exclusive licence to display its business information, logo and quotation content for the purpose of operating the Platform.</p>
<h2>16. Confidentiality &amp; data protection</h2><p>The Supplier shall keep any Customer information received strictly confidential and use it only to fulfil the specific job. Each party shall comply with UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 on the Protection of Personal Data (PDPL). QuotesDone processes the personal data of the Supplier and its representatives where necessary to perform this Agreement, and for these specified purposes: account management, identity and licence verification, subscription invoicing and collection, fraud and security monitoring, and service analytics. Processing necessary to operate this Agreement relies on contractual necessity rather than consent alone. Any separate purpose, such as marketing, will be based on separate consent. The Supplier and its representatives have the right to access, correct and request deletion of their personal data (PDPL Arts. 14–16) and may lodge a complaint with the UAE Data Office. Full details are set out in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, which is provided at the point of registration.</p>
<h2>17. Warranties &amp; disclaimers</h2><p>The Platform is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. QuotesDone does not warrant any volume of leads, quotations or jobs, uninterrupted availability, or that any Customer will proceed. To the extent permitted by law, all implied warranties are excluded.</p>
<h2>18. Limitation of liability &amp; indemnity</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by UAE law, QuotesDone, its owners, staff and affiliates shall not be liable for disputes between the Supplier and a Customer, loss of business or profit, or any indirect or consequential loss; and QuotesDone's total aggregate liability to the Supplier shall not exceed the fees the Supplier paid to QuotesDone in the 12 months before the claim. The Supplier shall indemnify QuotesDone against claims, losses and costs arising from the Supplier's work, breach of this Agreement, or breach of law. Nothing excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
<h2>19. Suspension &amp; termination</h2><p>QuotesDone may suspend or terminate access for breach of this Agreement, non-payment, expired licensing, or conduct harmful to the Platform or its users. The Supplier may stop using the Platform at any time. Outstanding Subscription Fees and charges survive termination and remain payable.</p>
<h2>20. Force majeure</h2><p>Neither party is liable for failure or delay caused by events beyond its reasonable control.</p>
<h2>21. Notices</h2><p>Notices to the Supplier may be sent to the registered email or shown in the supplier portal; notices to QuotesDone should be sent to management@quotesdone.com.</p>
<h2>22. General</h2><p>QuotesDone may assign this Agreement; the Supplier may not assign without consent. If any provision is held unenforceable, the remainder stands. No failure to enforce is a waiver. This Agreement, with the Privacy Policy and any fee notices, is the entire agreement between the parties.</p>
<h2>23. Amendments</h2><p>QuotesDone may update this Agreement and its fees. For material changes — in particular any increase in fees — QuotesDone will give at least <b>30 days' notice</b> and will ask the Supplier to re-confirm acceptance; a Supplier who does not accept a material change may terminate without penalty within the notice period. Non-material changes take effect when published on this page.</p>
<h2>24. No-circumvention of the Platform</h2><p>The Supplier acknowledges that any customer, project or lead made known to it through the Platform results directly from QuotesDone's introduction and is QuotesDone's protected commercial interest. For 24 months from such introduction, the Supplier shall not, directly or indirectly, conclude, invoice or facilitate any transaction with that customer for the same or similar scope outside the Platform with the purpose or effect of avoiding QuotesDone's fee. Each breach entitles QuotesDone to liquidated compensation of AED 15,000 per incident, or three (3) times the fee that would otherwise have been payable, whichever is higher, in addition to recovery of the unpaid fee.</p>
<h2>25. Confidentiality &amp; platform data</h2><p>All leads, customer details, anonymised scopes, pricing data and materials accessed through the Platform are confidential and remain the property of QuotesDone. The Supplier shall not copy, store, resell or reuse such data outside a transaction conducted on the Platform, nor supply it to any third party or competing service. Each proven breach entitles QuotesDone to liquidated compensation of AED 20,000 per incident, plus injunctive relief.</p>
<h2>26. No replication or competing use</h2><p>The Supplier shall not reproduce, reverse-engineer, or use QuotesDone's software, matching logic, anonymisation outputs or document templates to develop or assist any competing platform.</p>
<h2>27. AI-generated content and platform outputs</h2><p>The Platform uses automated and AI-based tools to extract bills of quantities from drawings, standardise and anonymise quotations, generate cost estimates and comparisons, and power support and category assistants. These outputs are provided for convenience only, may contain errors or omissions, and do not constitute professional, engineering, legal or financial advice. The Supplier must independently verify any such output before relying on it, and QuotesDone is not liable for any loss arising from reliance on automated outputs.</p>
<h2>28. Anonymisation and standardised quotations</h2><p>QuotesDone anonymises quotations and related materials on a reasonable-efforts basis. The Supplier remains responsible for ensuring its quotations, drawings and uploads do not contain identifying, contact or branding information intended to circumvent anonymity, and QuotesDone is not liable if anonymisation is imperfect. Where QuotesDone produces a standardised or reformatted version of a quotation, that version is a convenience copy only; the Supplier's original submission governs in the event of any discrepancy.</p>
<h2>29. No guarantee of leads or outcomes</h2><p>QuotesDone provides access to the Platform but does not guarantee that the Supplier will receive any inquiries, quotation opportunities, reveals or won work, nor any particular volume, value or return. Registration and continued use are provided without any representation as to results.</p>
<h2>30. Electronic acceptance, records and audit</h2><p>The Supplier agrees that ticking the acceptance box, clicking to accept, or continuing to use the Platform constitutes a valid and binding electronic acceptance of this Agreement under the laws of the United Arab Emirates. QuotesDone's records — including its acceptance logs and the signed acceptance certificate it generates — are admissible and, absent manifest error, conclusive evidence of the terms accepted and the time of acceptance. To enforce the anti-circumvention provisions, QuotesDone may request reasonable evidence that a Customer introduced through the Platform was not dealt with off-Platform, and the Supplier shall cooperate in good faith.</p>
<h2>31. Payments, currency and future fees</h2><p>All amounts under this Agreement are stated and payable in UAE Dirhams (AED) unless otherwise agreed. Any amount overdue accrues simple interest at nine percent (9%) per annum, or the maximum permitted by UAE law if lower; this is the only interest rate under this Agreement. Registration and subscription fees are addressed in sections 6 and 7, and no supplier commission is charged; QuotesDone reserves the right to introduce or vary such fees in future in accordance with the Amendments section.</p>
<h2>32. Compliance, communications and feedback</h2><p>The Supplier warrants that it is not subject to sanctions and that its funds and activities are lawful, and it will comply with applicable anti-money-laundering and sanctions laws. The Supplier consents to receive service, transactional and (unless opted out) promotional communications by email, SMS and WhatsApp, and may unsubscribe from promotional messages at any time. Any feedback or suggestions the Supplier provides may be used by QuotesDone freely and without obligation. QuotesDone may identify the Supplier as a participant on the Platform and use its name or logo as a reference, unless the Supplier opts out by written notice.</p>
<h2>33. Response obligation and non-response charge</h2><p>Once a Customer reveals the Supplier&#39;s contact details, the Supplier must respond to that Customer within five (5) working days of the Reveal, by the on-platform message thread, telephone, email or other reasonable means. QuotesDone tracks every Reveal from payment: if the Supplier has not responded within three (3) working days, QuotesDone chases the Supplier, copying the Customer; if there is still no response by the fifth (5th) working day, QuotesDone&#39;s CEO makes a final call to the Supplier. If the Supplier does not respond to that call and QuotesDone consequently refunds the Customer&#39;s Reveal Fee, the Supplier shall pay QuotesDone: (a) a non-response charge equal to that Reveal Fee (3% of the quoted value); (b) an administrative fee of AED 250; and (c) simple interest on the total at the clause 31 rate of nine percent (9%) per annum (or the maximum permitted by UAE law if lower), calculated from the date of the Customer&#39;s payment until settled. These amounts reflect QuotesDone&#39;s cost of the refund caused by the Supplier&#39;s non-response; they are payable within seven (7) days of QuotesDone&#39;s notice and may be recorded as a due on the Supplier&#39;s account. The Supplier is not matched to new Customers until the amount is settled. Repeated non-response may also lead to suspension or removal from the Platform.</p>
<h2>34. Governing law &amp; jurisdiction</h2><p>This Agreement is governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates, and the parties submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts of the Emirate of Dubai.</p>
<h2>35. Contact</h2><p>QuotesDone Technologies · Sole Establishment · Dubai DET E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275 · Commercial Register No. 2883503 · Dubai, United Arab Emirates · management@quotesdone.com · +971 50 931 9355</p>$qd_supplier_agreement$
 where slug = 'legal_supplier_body';

