update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_privacy$<h1>Privacy Policy</h1><div class="muted">How QuotesDone Technologies collects, uses, shares and protects personal data on the QuotesDone anonymous quotation marketplace, and your rights under UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 (the Personal Data Protection Law).</div><div class="card"><h2>1. Who We Are (Data Controller)</h2><p>This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your personal data when you use QuotesDone, an online B2B anonymous quotation marketplace.</p><p>The data controller is:</p><ul><li>QuotesDone Technologies, a Dubai Sole Establishment</li><li>Dubai DET E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275</li><li>Commercial Register No. 2883503</li><li>Owner: Ahmad Mhd Nabil Alzain</li><li>Address: Dubai, United Arab Emirates</li><li>Email: management@quotesdone.com; Phone: +971 50 931 9355 (the number on our licence record is +971 56 791 8605)</li></ul><p>We process personal data in accordance with the UAE Personal Data Protection Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 (PDPL), and its implementing regime overseen by the UAE Data Office, which from June 2026 operates within the new UAE Federal Authority for Artificial Intelligence and Data. This policy applies to customers, suppliers and visitors. Where you act on behalf of a business, references to your personal data mean the personal data of the individuals concerned.</p><h2>2. Personal Data We Collect</h2><p>Depending on how you use the platform, we collect:</p><ul><li>Customer identity and contact data: your name, email address and mobile number, with the mobile number verified by one-time password (OTP).</li><li>Request content: the job or request you submit as text, voice recordings, photographs or drawings, including any personal data you choose to include.</li><li>Supplier data: business details and Know Your Customer (KYC) documents provided for vetting and onboarding.</li><li>Payment data: a payment reference returned by our payment processor, Stripe. We do not store full card numbers; card and Apple Pay details are handled by Stripe, which is certified to the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS).</li><li>Usage and technical data: logs, device and connection information, and records of platform activity.</li></ul><p>We do not intentionally collect special categories of data. Please avoid including sensitive details in request content unless necessary.</p><h2>3. Purposes and Lawful Bases</h2><p>We process personal data for clear purposes, each supported by a lawful basis under the PDPL:</p><ul><li>To create and manage your account, verify your mobile by OTP, and provide the marketplace, including matching requests to suppliers and enabling paid reveals (performance of a contract).</li><li>To calculate and collect the customer Reveal Fee of 3% of the quoted value at the point you choose to reveal a supplier, and to keep accounting records (performance of a contract and legal obligation). Suppliers pay no commission or success fee on jobs they win.</li><li>To vet suppliers and verify KYC documents, prevent fraud and misuse, secure the platform and improve our services (legitimate interests).</li><li>To share a chosen supplier&#x27;s contact details on a paid reveal, and for optional marketing (your consent, which you may withdraw at any time).</li></ul><p>Where we rely on legitimate interests, we balance these against your rights and interests.</p><h2>4. AI and Automated Processing</h2><p>QuotesDone uses automated tools, including artificial intelligence, to operate the marketplace. These tools:</p><ul><li>Structure and standardise the requests you submit (including converting voice, photos and drawings into a structured brief).</li><li>Match each request to vetted suppliers likely to be able to quote.</li><li>Summarise requests and quotes to make them easier to compare.</li></ul><p>This automated processing supports our service but does not produce binding legal effects on you without human involvement, and you remain free to accept, reject or ignore any quote. You may contact us to ask questions about, or object to, automated processing as described in the Your Rights section. Where automated processing could significantly affect individuals, we assess its impact before deploying it.</p><h2>5. How We Share Data</h2><p>Anonymity is central to QuotesDone. We share personal data only as follows:</p><ul><li>Request content is shared with matched suppliers WITHOUT revealing your identity, so suppliers can prepare anonymised quotes.</li><li>Your contact details are disclosed to a single supplier only after you pay the Reveal Fee and consent to the reveal for that chosen supplier; suppliers receive customer contact data only for jobs revealed to them.</li><li>Our payment processor, Stripe, receives the data needed to take payment (card or Apple Pay) and returns a payment reference.</li><li>Service providers (such as hosting, communications and analytics) process data on our behalf under written instructions.</li></ul><p>We may also disclose data where required by UAE law, a court of competent authority, or to protect our legal rights. We do not sell personal data.</p><h2>6. Cross-Border Transfers</h2><p>Some of our service providers may process personal data outside the United Arab Emirates. Where this happens, we apply the safeguards required by Articles 22 and 23 of the PDPL.</p><ul><li>We transfer data to countries the UAE Data Office recognises as providing an adequate level of protection; or</li><li>Where adequacy is not established, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as contractual clauses obliging the recipient to protect the data to UAE standards, or on your explicit consent, in each case in a manner that does not conflict with the public and security interests of the State.</li></ul><p>You may contact us for more information about the specific safeguards applied to a transfer.</p><h2>7. Data Retention</h2><p>We keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described above and to meet legal obligations.</p><ul><li>Account data is kept while your account is active and for a reasonable period afterwards.</li><li>Request content is retained to operate and improve matching, then deleted or anonymised when no longer needed.</li><li>Transaction and financial records, including Reveal Fee and registration-fee records, are retained for the periods required by UAE accounting and tax law.</li><li>Supplier KYC documents are retained for the duration of the relationship and any legally required period thereafter.</li><li>Logs are kept for limited periods for security and audit purposes.</li></ul><p>When a retention period ends, we securely delete or irreversibly anonymise the data. Our internal Data Protection and Retention Policy sets out the detailed schedule.</p><h2>8. Your Rights Under the PDPL</h2><p>Subject to the conditions and exceptions in the PDPL, you have the right to:</p><ul><li>Access your personal data and obtain information about how it is processed.</li><li>Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li><li>Request deletion of your data where the legal grounds apply.</li><li>Object to, or request restriction of, certain processing, including processing based on legitimate interests and certain automated processing.</li><li>Request that your personal data be provided to you, or transferred to another controller, in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format (data portability), where technically feasible.</li><li>Request that your data be transferred to you or another controller in a structured format, where applicable.</li><li>Withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing carried out before withdrawal.</li></ul><p>To exercise any right, contact us at management@quotesdone.com. We will respond within the timeframes required by the PDPL. If you are not satisfied, you may lodge a complaint with the UAE Data Office.</p><h2>9. Electronic Marketing and Communications</h2><p>We send transactional messages you need to use the service — for example mobile one-time passwords (OTP), request and quote notifications, and account or payment confirmations — on the basis of our contract with you; these are not marketing.</p><p>We send marketing or promotional messages by email, SMS or other electronic means only where you have given consent, and you can withdraw consent or unsubscribe at any time using the link or instructions in the message, or by emailing management@quotesdone.com. We handle electronic communications in line with the UAE telecommunications and electronic-marketing rules overseen by the Telecommunications and Digital Government Regulatory Authority (TDRA) and the Electronic Transactions and Trust Services Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021). We do not sell your contact details for third-party marketing.</p><h2>10. Security</h2><p>We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against unauthorised access, loss, alteration or disclosure, consistent with the PDPL and the Electronic Transactions and Trust Services Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021.</p><ul><li>Access to personal data is restricted to authorised personnel on a need-to-know basis.</li><li>We use encryption in transit, OTP verification for customer mobile numbers, and segregation of anonymised request content from identity data.</li><li>Payment card data is handled by Stripe, our PCI DSS–certified payment processor, and is not stored by us.</li></ul><p>No system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. If a personal data breach occurs that meets the legal threshold, we will notify the UAE Data Office and affected individuals as required by the PDPL.</p><h2>11. Children, Changes and Contact</h2><p>QuotesDone is a business-to-business platform intended for users aged 18 and over. It is not directed at minors, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe a minor has provided us data, please contact us so we can delete it.</p><p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our services or the law. The current version is always available on our platform, and material changes will be notified where appropriate.</p><p>For any privacy question, to exercise your rights, or to reach our data protection contact, please use:</p><ul><li>Email: management@quotesdone.com</li><li>Phone: +971 50 931 9355 (licence record: +971 56 791 8605)</li><li>Post: QuotesDone Technologies, Dubai, United Arab Emirates (our DET E-Trader portal licence is for an online business with no shop front, so there is no street address)</li></ul><p>This policy is governed by the laws of the UAE, and disputes are subject to the courts of Dubai.</p></div>$qd_privacy$
 where slug = 'privacy';

update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_refund_policy$<h1>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1><div class="muted">Explains when the QuotesDone Reveal Fee is and is not refundable, how to request a refund, processing times and method, supplier registration-fee terms, and your preserved statutory rights under UAE Federal Law No. 15 of 2020.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. About This Policy</h2><p>This Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy applies to QuotesDone, an online business-to-business quotation marketplace operated by QuotesDone Technologies (Dubai Sole Establishment; Dubai DET E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275; Commercial Register No. 2883503), Dubai, United Arab Emirates.</p><p>QuotesDone is a marketplace and facilitator only. We connect customers with suppliers and provide anonymised quotations. We are not a contractor, supplier or party to the works quoted, and this Policy governs only the fees you pay to QuotesDone, not amounts payable to a supplier under any separate contract you enter into.</p><p>This Policy must be read together with our Terms &amp; Conditions. It is governed by the laws of the UAE and applied without prejudice to your non-waivable statutory rights under Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection and its Implementing Regulation (Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023).</p><h2>2. The Reveal Fee</h2><p>To unlock the identity and contact details of a chosen supplier behind an anonymised quotation, you pay a Reveal Fee equal to 3% of the quoted amount. No cap applies to the Reveal Fee.</p><p>The Reveal Fee is a charge for the reveal service provided by QuotesDone. It is separate from, and additional to, any price agreed between you and the supplier for the actual goods, services or works.</p><p>Because the Reveal Fee unlocks supplier information immediately on payment, it is generally treated as earned once the reveal is delivered, subject to the specific refund right described below and to your statutory rights under UAE law.</p><h2>3. When the Reveal Fee Is Refundable</h2><p>We refund the Reveal Fee in one defined circumstance: where a revealed supplier does not respond to you within five (5) working days of your payment and does not respond to QuotesDone&#39;s CEO&#39;s final call. You do not need to prove anything for the clock to start: we track every reveal from the moment you pay. If the supplier has not responded within three (3) working days, we chase the supplier on your behalf and copy you; if there is still no response on the fifth (5th) working day, the case goes to QuotesDone&#39;s CEO for a final call; if the supplier does not respond to that call, the refund is issued.</p><p>If you have tried to reach the supplier yourself, dated copies of emails, messages sent through the Platform, or call logs help us close the case faster, but they are not a condition of the refund. Working days are Monday to Friday, excluding UAE public holidays.</p><p>If these conditions are met, the Reveal Fee for that supplier is refunded in full. The CEO&#39;s decision, whichever way it goes, is recorded against your refund case reference and the decision reference, and both are shown to you in your account and quoted when we confirm the outcome. This refund right is in addition to any remedy available to you under Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection.</p><h2>4. When the Reveal Fee Is Not Refundable</h2><p>The Reveal Fee is not refundable once the revealed supplier has responded to you within the five-working-day window, as the reveal service has then been fully delivered and the supplier has engaged.</p><p>The Reveal Fee is not refundable for a change of mind, for example where you decide not to proceed with a supplier who did respond, where you select a different supplier, or where the supplier&#x27;s pricing or terms no longer suit you.</p><p>The Reveal Fee is not refundable where the supplier responded to you or to QuotesDone within the five-working-day window. Nothing in this section limits your non-waivable rights under UAE consumer protection law where they apply.</p><h2>5. How to Request a Refund</h2><p>You do not need to submit a request for a non-response refund: the ladder above runs automatically from the moment you pay. You can still tell us at any time that the supplier is not responding, by emailing management@quotesdone.com or by using the support function on the Platform, and we will chase the supplier immediately.</p><p>If you do write to us, your account email and the reveal reference are enough. Proof of your own attempts to reach the supplier (emails, Platform messages or call logs) is optional: it can help us close the case faster, but it is never a condition of the refund (see section 3).</p><p>We may ask for further information to identify your reveal. Providing complete and accurate information helps us assess and process eligible refunds promptly.</p><h2>6. Processing Time and Method</h2><p>Once QuotesDone&#39;s CEO decides a refund, it is issued to the original payment method through our payment processor, Stripe, and we confirm it to you with your refund case reference. Banks and card issuers usually take seven (7) to fourteen (14) working days to show the refund on your statement.</p><p><b>Payments handled by Stripe · PCI DSS.</b> Your card or Apple Pay payment is processed by Stripe, a payment processor certified to the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard; QuotesDone never sees or stores your full card number.</p><p>Refunds are made in the currency of the original payment and for the full Reveal Fee you paid. QuotesDone does not deduct an administrative charge from your refund. The administrative fee of AED 250 and the interest at 9% per annum that QuotesDone charges under the Supplier Agreement are charged to the supplier whose non-response caused the refund, never to you.</p><p>If a refund cannot be returned to the original payment method for reasons outside our control, we will agree an alternative lawful method with you.</p><h2>7. Supplier Registration-Fee Terms</h2><p>Suppliers may be charged a registration fee to join and maintain a profile on the Platform. QuotesDone charges suppliers no commission, success fee or transaction fee on jobs they win. These terms apply to suppliers, not to customers.</p><p>Any supplier registration fee is charged for access to the marketplace and listing services over the registration period. Where a fee covers a defined period, it is generally non-refundable for the unused portion once access has been granted, except where required by law or expressly agreed in writing.</p><h2>8. Your Statutory Rights</h2><p>Nothing in this Policy excludes, restricts or waives any right you may have under Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection and its Implementing Regulation (Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023), or under other applicable UAE law.</p><p>Where a service is not provided as described, your statutory remedies under UAE consumer protection law continue to apply alongside the contractual refund right in this Policy.</p><p>If you believe your consumer rights have not been honoured, you may contact us first and, if unresolved, escalate to the relevant authority as set out in our Complaints &amp; Dispute Resolution Policy.</p></div>$qd_refund_policy$
 where slug = 'refund-policy';

update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_cookie_policy$<h1>Cookie Policy</h1><div class="muted">How QuotesDone uses cookies and similar technologies, how we obtain consent consistent with UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021, and how you can manage or disable them.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. About This Policy</h2><p>This Cookie Policy explains how QuotesDone Technologies (Dubai DET E-Trader Licence No. 1633275) uses cookies and similar technologies on the QuotesDone platform. It should be read together with our Privacy Policy.</p><p>Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. Similar technologies include local storage, pixels and tags that perform comparable functions.</p><p>Where cookies collect or relate to personal data, we handle that data in accordance with the UAE Personal Data Protection Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 (PDPL). This policy tells you which cookies we use, why, and how you can control them. By using the platform after being shown our cookie notice, and where required after giving consent, you agree to the use of cookies as described here.</p><h2>2. Cookies We Use</h2><p>We use the following categories:</p><ul><li>Essential and session cookies: necessary to run the platform, keep you signed in, remember your request as you build it, and enable core features such as paid reveals. The platform cannot function properly without these.</li><li>Security cookies: help us verify sessions, support OTP-based mobile verification, detect fraud and protect the platform and your account.</li><li>Analytics cookies: help us understand how the platform is used so we can improve performance and matching. These may be set by trusted analytics providers and are used in an aggregated or pseudonymised manner where possible.</li></ul><p>We do not use cookies to build advertising profiles or to sell your data.</p><h2>3. Consent Approach</h2><p>Our approach to cookie consent is consistent with the PDPL:</p><ul><li>Essential and security cookies are strictly necessary for the service and are set without requiring separate consent, because they are required to deliver the service you request.</li><li>Analytics and other non-essential cookies are only used where we have an appropriate lawful basis, and where consent is required we obtain it through our cookie notice before those cookies are set.</li><li>You can accept or decline non-essential cookies, and you can change your choice at any time.</li></ul><p>Withdrawing consent or declining non-essential cookies will not prevent you from using the core features of QuotesDone, although some functionality and our ability to improve the service may be affected.</p><h2>4. Managing and Disabling Cookies</h2><p>You can control cookies in several ways:</p><ul><li>Use the cookie notice or settings on our platform to accept or decline non-essential categories and to update your preferences.</li><li>Adjust your browser settings to block or delete cookies, or to warn you before cookies are stored. Most browsers allow this through their privacy or settings menu.</li><li>Use your device or browser&#x27;s controls for local storage and similar technologies.</li></ul><p>Please note that blocking essential or security cookies may stop parts of the platform from working, including sign-in, request submission and paid reveals. Disabling analytics cookies will not affect core functionality.</p><p>For help managing cookies, contact us at management@quotesdone.com.</p><h2>5. Third-Party Tags</h2><p>Some cookies and tags are set by third parties that provide services to us:</p><ul><li>Analytics providers, which help us measure and improve how the platform performs.</li><li>Our payment processor, Stripe, which may set cookies or use similar technologies to process card and Apple Pay payments securely and to prevent payment fraud during the reveal and payment flows.</li></ul><p>These third parties process data under their own terms and policies and, where they act for us, under written instructions. We share only what is needed for the relevant service. We encourage you to review the privacy and cookie notices of any third-party services you interact with through the platform.</p><h2>6. Changes and Contact</h2><p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the technologies we use or in applicable law. The current version is always available on our platform, and the effective date will be updated when we make changes.</p><p>If you have any questions about our use of cookies or wish to exercise your data protection rights under the PDPL, please contact:</p><ul><li>QuotesDone Technologies</li><li>Email: management@quotesdone.com</li><li>Phone: +971 50 931 9355 (licence record: +971 56 791 8605)</li><li>Address: Dubai, United Arab Emirates</li></ul><p>This policy is governed by the laws of the UAE, and any disputes are subject to the courts of Dubai.</p></div>$qd_cookie_policy$
 where slug = 'cookie-policy';

update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_acceptable_use$<h1>Acceptable Use Policy</h1><div class="muted">Defines permitted and prohibited conduct on the QuotesDone Platform, including accuracy of information, prohibitions on fraud, abuse, scraping, circumvention, IP infringement and off-platform identification of suppliers before reveal, the consequences of breach, and how to report misuse.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. About This Policy</h2><p>This Acceptable Use Policy applies to all users of QuotesDone, operated by QuotesDone Technologies (Dubai Sole Establishment; Dubai DET E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275; Commercial Register No. 2883503), Dubai, United Arab Emirates.</p><p>By accessing or using the Platform, you agree to use it lawfully and in line with this Policy, our Terms &amp; Conditions and applicable UAE law.</p><p>This Policy supports the integrity of the anonymous-quotation model, which depends on accurate information and on supplier identities remaining protected until a Reveal Fee is paid.</p><h2>2. Permitted Conduct</h2><p>You may use QuotesDone to request, receive and compare anonymised quotations, to pay the applicable Reveal Fee to unlock a chosen supplier, and to communicate with suppliers for genuine, lawful business purposes.</p><p>You must provide accurate, current and complete information when registering, submitting requirements and requesting quotations, and keep your account details up to date.</p><p>You must keep your login credentials secure and are responsible for activity carried out under your account.</p><h2>3. Prohibited Conduct</h2><p>You must not use the Platform for any unlawful, fraudulent or deceptive purpose, submit false, misleading or fictitious requests or quotations, or impersonate any person or business.</p><p>You must not abuse, harass, threaten or defame other users or our staff, post unlawful, infringing or offensive content, or upload malware or anything that could harm the Platform or its users.</p><p>You must not infringe the intellectual property or other rights of QuotesDone or any third party, including by copying, reproducing or exploiting Platform content without authorisation.</p><h2>4. No Scraping or Circumvention</h2><p>You must not scrape, harvest, crawl, data-mine or use automated means to extract data from the Platform, nor attempt to access areas, accounts or data you are not authorised to access.</p><p>You must not interfere with or circumvent the security, anonymisation, payment or reveal mechanisms of the Platform, or take any action designed to avoid paying the Reveal Fee.</p><p>You must not reverse engineer, disrupt, overload or otherwise compromise the Platform&#x27;s normal operation.</p><h2>5. Protecting Supplier Anonymity</h2><p>The Platform anonymises supplier identities until you pay the Reveal Fee. You must not attempt to identify, contact or deal with a supplier off-platform before reveal, including by deducing or researching a supplier&#x27;s identity from a quotation.</p><p>You must not, after a reveal, deal with a supplier in a way designed to deprive QuotesDone of the Reveal Fee, such as deliberately taking a transaction off the Platform to avoid charges.</p><p>These rules protect the fairness of the marketplace for both customers and suppliers and form an essential condition of using the Platform.</p><h2>6. Consequences of Breach</h2><p>If you breach this Policy, we may, at our discretion and proportionate to the breach, issue a warning, restrict features, suspend or terminate your account, remove content, or withhold a reveal.</p><p>Serious or unlawful conduct, including fraud, circumvention of fees, intellectual property infringement or unlawful content, may result in legal action and referral to the competent UAE authorities.</p><p>We may retain and use relevant records as evidence to the extent permitted by Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 on the Protection of Personal Data and other applicable UAE law.</p><h2>7. Reporting Misuse</h2><p>If you become aware of any breach of this Policy, suspected fraud, security vulnerability or other misuse of the Platform, please report it to us at management@quotesdone.com or through the Platform&#x27;s reporting function.</p><p>Please include enough detail to allow us to investigate, such as the accounts, quotations or messages involved and any supporting evidence.</p><p>We take reports seriously, investigate appropriately, and may cooperate with the competent UAE authorities where required by law.</p></div>$qd_acceptable_use$
 where slug = 'acceptable-use';

update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_disclaimer$<h1>Disclaimer &amp; Limitation of Liability</h1><div class="muted">Confirms QuotesDone&#x27;s marketplace/intermediary status, exactly which supplier checks QuotesDone performs and the absence of warranties beyond them on quality, pricing or completion, your due-diligence responsibility, and a limitation of liability to fees paid, with carve-outs for fraud, gross negligence and non-waivable UAE consumer and legal rights.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. About This Disclaimer</h2><p>This Disclaimer &amp; Limitation of Liability applies to QuotesDone, operated by QuotesDone Technologies (Dubai Sole Establishment; Dubai DET E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275; Commercial Register No. 2883503), Dubai, United Arab Emirates.</p><p>It forms part of our Terms &amp; Conditions and should be read together with our Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy and Complaints &amp; Dispute Resolution Policy.</p><p>It is governed by the laws of the UAE, including Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection, the Federal Decree-Law No. 50 of 2022 on Commercial Transactions and the Civil Transactions Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 25 of 2025), and is applied subject to your non-waivable statutory rights.</p><h2>2. Marketplace / Intermediary Status</h2><p>QuotesDone is an online marketplace and intermediary that provides anonymised supplier quotations and a reveal service. We are not a contractor, supplier, agent or party to any contract for goods, services or works formed between a customer and a supplier.</p><p>Any contract for the actual goods, services or works is entered into directly between the customer and the chosen supplier, on terms agreed between them. We are not responsible for performing, supervising or guaranteeing that contract.</p><p>Our role is limited to operating the Platform and facilitating connections between customers and suppliers.</p><h2>3. No Warranty on Suppliers or Quotes</h2><p>Before a supplier can be matched, QuotesDone checks the mandatory six (business name, mobile number, email address, trade licence, company profile and signed Supplier Agreement) and, on the trade licence, the licence number, issuing authority and expiry date, as published at <a href="/how-we-verify/">How we verify suppliers</a>. That is what &quot;verified&quot; and &quot;licence-checked&quot; mean on QuotesDone. The check confirms the licence as presented on the date it was made; it does not guarantee that the licence covers your specific works.</p><p>Beyond those checks, we do not warrant or guarantee the qualifications, conduct, workmanship, solvency, insurance, quality, pricing, availability or completion of any supplier or the works they quote for.</p><p>Quotations provided through the Platform are indicative only. Final scope, price and terms are a matter for direct agreement between you and the supplier, and may differ from the indicative quote.</p><p>While we take reasonable steps to operate the Platform properly, the Platform and its content are provided on an &quot;as is&quot; and &quot;as available&quot; basis to the extent permitted by UAE law.</p><h2>4. Customer Due-Diligence Responsibility</h2><p>You are responsible for carrying out your own due diligence on any supplier before entering into a contract, including confirming that their trade licence covers your specific works and checking permits, insurance, references, pricing and suitability for your requirements.</p><p>You should satisfy yourself as to the terms of any contract you enter into with a supplier and should not rely on QuotesDone to assess or approve the supplier on your behalf.</p><p>Paying the Reveal Fee unlocks supplier contact details; it is not an endorsement or recommendation of the supplier. The only verification QuotesDone performs is the one described at <a href="/how-we-verify/">How we verify suppliers</a>; everything beyond it, including whether the licence covers your specific works, permits, insurance and references, remains yours to check.</p><h2>5. Limitation of Liability</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by UAE law, our total aggregate liability to you arising out of or in connection with the Platform and our services is limited to the total fees you have actually paid to QuotesDone for the relevant transaction giving rise to the claim.</p><p>To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss, loss of profit, loss of business or loss of opportunity, or for the acts, omissions, defaults or insolvency of any supplier.</p><p>These limitations reflect the nature of QuotesDone as a marketplace intermediary and the fees charged for our reveal service.</p><h2>6. Carve-Outs and Non-Waivable Rights</h2><p>Nothing in this Disclaimer excludes or limits our liability for fraud, fraudulent misrepresentation, gross negligence or wilful misconduct, or for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, or for any other liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p><p>Nothing in this Disclaimer excludes, restricts or waives any non-waivable right or remedy you have under Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection and its Implementing Regulation (Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023), or under other mandatory provisions of UAE law.</p><p>Where any provision of this Disclaimer is found to be unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue in full force and effect.</p></div>$qd_disclaimer$
 where slug = 'disclaimer';

update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_complaints_policy$<h1>Complaints &amp; Dispute Resolution Policy</h1><div class="muted">Sets out how to raise a complaint with QuotesDone, our acknowledgement and resolution timelines, the escalation path, our facilitation-only role in customer-supplier disputes, and your right to escalate to the relevant UAE authority and the courts of Dubai.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. About This Policy</h2><p>This Complaints &amp; Dispute Resolution Policy applies to QuotesDone, operated by QuotesDone Technologies (Dubai Sole Establishment; Dubai DET E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275; Commercial Register No. 2883503), Dubai, United Arab Emirates.</p><p>We are committed to handling complaints fairly, promptly and in line with Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection and its Implementing Regulation (Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023).</p><p>This Policy explains how to raise a complaint about the QuotesDone Platform or our services, how we respond, and your rights to escalate, including to the relevant UAE authority and the courts of Dubai.</p><h2>2. How to Raise a Complaint</h2><p>You can raise a complaint by emailing management@quotesdone.com or by sending a message marked as a complaint through our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. Every complaint receives a ticket number, and you can follow its status (acknowledged, in review, final response) at <a href="/complaints/status/">quotesdone.com/complaints/status</a> using the ticket number and your email address.</p><p>To help us assist you quickly, please include your name and account details, the relevant quotation, reveal or supplier reference, a clear description of the issue, the outcome you are seeking, and any supporting evidence such as emails, Platform messages, screenshots or receipts.</p><p>We treat all complaints confidentially and handle personal data in accordance with Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 on the Protection of Personal Data and our Privacy Policy.</p><h2>3. Acknowledgement and Resolution Timelines</h2><p>We aim to acknowledge your complaint within two (2) working days of receipt and to provide a substantive response or resolution within ten (10) working days.</p><p>Where a complaint is complex or requires information from a third party, we will tell you and provide a revised timeframe, keeping you updated on progress.</p><p>Working days exclude Saturdays, Sundays and UAE public holidays. We maintain records of complaints and their outcomes to help us improve our service.</p><h2>4. Our Role in Customer-Supplier Disputes</h2><p>QuotesDone is a marketplace and facilitator only. We are not a contractor, supplier or party to any contract for goods, services or works formed between a customer and a supplier through the Platform.</p><p>Where a dispute concerns the supplier&#x27;s quote, pricing, quality, licensing, conduct or completion of works, that is a matter between you and the supplier. Our role is limited to reasonable facilitation, such as sharing relevant Platform records or helping reconnect the parties.</p><p>Complaints that relate to the QuotesDone Platform itself, such as the Reveal Fee, the reveal service or account matters, are handled directly by us under this Policy.</p><h2>5. Escalation Path</h2><p>If you are not satisfied with our initial response, you may ask for your complaint to be reviewed by QuotesDone&#39;s CEO by replying to our response or emailing management@quotesdone.com and marking your message for escalation.</p><p>We will conduct a further review and aim to provide a final written response, setting out our position and the reasons for it, together with the external escalation routes in section 6.</p><p>If the matter remains unresolved after this internal escalation, you may pursue the external options described below.</p><h2>6. Escalating to UAE Authorities</h2><p>Because QuotesDone is licensed in Dubai, you may refer an unresolved consumer complaint to the Department of Economy and Tourism (DET) in Dubai through its Consumer Protection / Consumer Rights channels (including the Dubai Consumer App and website).</p><p>You may also contact the UAE Ministry of Economy consumer protection service, including its consumer hotline (800 1222), which receives and coordinates consumer complaints with the competent authorities.</p><p>These authorities handle complaints under Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection and its Implementing Regulation (Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023). Referring a matter to them does not affect your other legal rights.</p><h2>7. Governing Law and Courts</h2><p>This Policy and any dispute arising from your use of QuotesDone are governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates, including the Federal Decree-Law No. 50 of 2022 on Commercial Transactions and the Civil Transactions Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 25 of 2025) where applicable.</p><p>Subject to any mandatory consumer protection provisions and to the authority referral options above, the courts of Dubai have jurisdiction over disputes between you and QuotesDone.</p><p>Nothing in this Policy prevents you from exercising any non-waivable statutory right or from seeking the remedies available to you under applicable UAE law.</p></div>$qd_complaints_policy$
 where slug = 'complaints-policy';

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. version, date and hash of all eight
update public.legal_documents
   set version = 'v6', effective_date = date '2026-09-14',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'customer-terms';
update public.legal_documents
   set version = 'v9', effective_date = date '2026-09-14',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'supplier-agreement';
update public.legal_documents
   set version = '1.3', effective_date = date '2026-09-14',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'privacy';
update public.legal_documents
   set version = '1.4', effective_date = date '2026-09-14',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'refund-policy';
update public.legal_documents
   set version = '1.2', effective_date = date '2026-09-14',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'cookie-policy';
update public.legal_documents
   set version = '1.2', effective_date = date '2026-09-14',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'acceptable-use';
update public.legal_documents
   set version = '1.1', effective_date = date '2026-09-14',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'disclaimer';
update public.legal_documents
   set version = '1.2', effective_date = date '2026-09-14',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'complaints-policy';

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4. the terms pins and labels follow the registry
update public.app_secrets set value = (select encode(sha256(convert_to(html, 'UTF8')), 'hex') from public.pages where slug = 'legal_terms_body'), updated_at = now()
 where key = 'terms_sha256_customer';
update public.app_secrets set value = (select version from public.legal_documents where slug = 'customer-terms'), updated_at = now()
 where key in ('customer_terms_version', 'terms_sha256_customer_version');
update public.app_secrets set value = (select encode(sha256(convert_to(html, 'UTF8')), 'hex') from public.pages where slug = 'legal_supplier_body'), updated_at = now()
 where key = 'terms_sha256_supplier';
update public.app_secrets set value = (select version from public.legal_documents where slug = 'supplier-agreement'), updated_at = now()
 where key in ('terms_version', 'supplier_terms_version', 'terms_sha256_supplier_version');
update public.app_secrets s
   set value = d.title || ' — Version ' || ltrim(d.version, 'vV'), updated_at = now()
  from public.legal_documents d
 where s.key = 'customer_terms_label' and d.slug = 'customer-terms';
update public.app_secrets s
   set value = 'Supplier Agreement — Version ' || ltrim(d.version, 'vV'), updated_at = now()
  from public.legal_documents d
 where s.key = 'supplier_terms_label' and d.slug = 'supplier-agreement';

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5. the file proves what the check will read
-- The expected hashes were computed by the generator from legal.json; a byte lost in quoting fails here.
do $check$
declare r record; n int; v text;
begin
  for r in select * from (values
    ('customer-terms', 'v6', date '2026-09-14', 'ab29c0a0dfd8db23b9f3c415cc74a61d3ea57860384c4aa4887f988076520c70'),
    ('supplier-agreement', 'v9', date '2026-09-14', 'abc1716c3003b8f0fbf19ff2f21eec6b97612ab4e50f8925d9977bae206963d2'),
    ('privacy', '1.3', date '2026-09-14', 'a90a2eb9a695f6ff5d06f1b9b7f8ce8eac67789d66ba129fd6fa0f207ec87b3a'),
    ('refund-policy', '1.4', date '2026-09-14', '9a3dcff0abb7e4cc90f4bc32338992da8795065cce54dd8eb39be2db1ed05072'),
    ('cookie-policy', '1.2', date '2026-09-14', 'b54b973282b074a90c02e73dec59c04f8e01695e7cb98ea11b69ffdb82c4c919'),
    ('acceptable-use', '1.2', date '2026-09-14', '222b306c4c07f8191d1e0cf5c96c4a16fb98c6878c227c2f27f12a7a9b1807c0'),
    ('disclaimer', '1.1', date '2026-09-14', '341ded99c33ce662d90a9944e5e27a177638adc20b2576c8774bdf452613c1ba'),
    ('complaints-policy', '1.2', date '2026-09-14', 'e692a02be83f93d3f6f31d8c90a6b1da4d0a75dd4aaac3136c3331d6d28edc24')
  ) as t(slug, version, eff, sha) loop
    select count(*) into n from public.legal_documents d
     where d.slug = r.slug and d.version = r.version and d.effective_date = r.eff
       and d.content_sha256 = r.sha and encode(sha256(convert_to(d.body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex') = r.sha;
    if n <> 1 then raise exception 'legal_documents.% is not % / % / %', r.slug, r.version, r.eff, r.sha; end if;
  end loop;

  -- test 2: every signed body names the registry version, and both agreements are in the join
  select count(*) into n from (
    select d.slug, d.version, (regexp_matches(p.html, 'Version (v?[0-9]+)', 'g'))[1] as named
      from public.legal_documents d join public.pages p on p.slug = replace(d.source, 'pages:', '')
     where d.source like 'pages:%') x
   where ltrim(x.named, 'vV') <> ltrim(x.version, 'vV');
  if n <> 0 then raise exception '% signed-body version label(s) disagree with the registry', n; end if;
  select count(distinct d.slug) into n
    from public.legal_documents d join public.pages p on p.slug = replace(d.source, 'pages:', '')
   where d.source like 'pages:%' and p.html ~ 'Version (v?[0-9]+)';
  if n < 2 then raise exception 'only % agreement(s) name a version in their signed body', n; end if;

  -- test 2: the pins, the live signed bodies and the published pages agree, and none is null
  if exists (
    with s as (
      select (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'terms_version') dv,
             (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'terms_sha256_supplier_version') pv,
             (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'terms_sha256_supplier') psha,
             (select encode(sha256(convert_to(value, 'UTF8')), 'hex') from public.app_secrets where key = 'supplier_terms_html') lsha,
             (select encode(sha256(convert_to(html, 'UTF8')), 'hex') from public.pages where slug = 'legal_supplier_body') pubsha
      union all
      select (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'customer_terms_version'),
             (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'terms_sha256_customer_version'),
             (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'terms_sha256_customer'),
             (select encode(sha256(convert_to(html, 'UTF8')), 'hex') from public.pages where slug = 'legal_terms_body'),
             (select encode(sha256(convert_to(html, 'UTF8')), 'hex') from public.pages where slug = 'legal_terms_body'))
    select 1 from s
     where dv is null or pv is null or psha is null or lsha is null or pubsha is null
        or psha <> lsha or dv <> pv or pubsha <> lsha)
  then raise exception 'terms pins are not intact'; end if;
  if (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'terms_sha256_customer') <> 'ab29c0a0dfd8db23b9f3c415cc74a61d3ea57860384c4aa4887f988076520c70' then raise exception 'customer pin is not the generated body'; end if;
  if (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'terms_sha256_supplier') <> 'abc1716c3003b8f0fbf19ff2f21eec6b97612ab4e50f8925d9977bae206963d2' then raise exception 'supplier pin is not the generated body'; end if;
  if (select value from public.app_secrets where key = 'supplier_terms_version') <> 'v9' then raise exception 'supplier_terms_version did not follow'; end if;

  -- the certificate caption names the version the acceptance row stores
  select value into v from public.app_secrets where key = 'customer_terms_label';
  if v not like '%Version 6' then raise exception 'customer_terms_label is %', v; end if;
  select value into v from public.app_secrets where key = 'supplier_terms_label';
  if v not like '%Version 9' then raise exception 'supplier_terms_label is %', v; end if;

  raise notice 'registry follows the 14 Sep texts: %', 'customer-terms v6, supplier-agreement v9, privacy 1.3, refund-policy 1.4, cookie-policy 1.2, acceptable-use 1.2, disclaimer 1.1, complaints-policy 1.2';
end
$check$;

commit;
